WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:01.540
How are you, did you have a good weekend?

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:02.710
Yeah, I did.
Everything's good?

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:03.810
Mm-hmm.
Life is fine?

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.950
Very good.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.460
'Cause I've been hard at work, you know?

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.293
[Andy] Oh, that's right.

00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:09.220
(laughs) You don't care at all.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.410
I mean--
This is true.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.010
You know, a lot of people, I'm
constantly thinking of ways

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.810
to make the show more exciting and dynamic

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.010
in whatever way I can
before we give up completely

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.450
and get into the auto business.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.283
[Andy] Mm-hmm.

00:00:20.283 --> 00:00:22.460
And anyway, what I thought I'd do

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.480
is the big thing today are psychics.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.500
Psychics are the big thing.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.464
You know, there's the psychic
hotline, psychic friends.

00:00:27.464 --> 00:00:28.810
Everyone's talking about psychics.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.490
Psychics make up half the guests
on the daytime talk shows.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:32.323
[Andy] It's true.

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:35.010
And so I thought, let's
do something with psychics

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.210
on this show, so ladies
and gentlemen, I went out

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.970
into New York City and I actually talked

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.600
to all of the most prominent psychics

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.410
that we could find in the Yellow Pages

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:47.450
to try and find out anything
we could just about,

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.980
are these people legit?
Yeah.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.840
How's the show gonna
be doing in the future?

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.110
What's gonna happen?

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.190
And we found out some
pretty impressive stuff.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:56.700
So ladies and gentlemen, enjoy my visit

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.450
with the psychics of New York City.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.370
Okay, I'm sitting here right now

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.550
with Astounding Velma, is that correct?

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:06.610
Velma, V-E-L-M-A, Velma.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.710
V-E, Velma.
You got it.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.879
And it's astounding.
I'm very astounding.

00:01:10.879 --> 00:01:12.210
Hmm.
I always have been.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.790
And you are a palmist, is that right?

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.590
I'm a palmist, I do magic, I do palmistry,

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.240
and I do a mind reading act

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.650
which we call transmission of thoughts.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.220
Hmm, so this is the human hand right here.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.170
Yeah, now, these lines actually,

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:26.230
this one happens to be the line of heart,

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.150
the line of emotions.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.370
[Conan] This is the heart line right here.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:31.422
Uh-huh, this is the line
of head, intelligence.

00:01:31.422 --> 00:01:33.230
This is the line of success.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:36.280
This is the line of life, but
there are many other aspects.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.810
This is the line of--
You got it.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:38.942
Tic-tac-toe.
No.

00:01:38.942 --> 00:01:41.110
I'll go first, then you.
(audience laughing)

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.530
Here we go, wait a
minute, what about here?

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.133
Oh, interesting, and then I'll go here.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.630
And I'll go--
(screams) No!

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.660
[Psychic] A light-haired
female will come into your life

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.610
that you'll care about.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.592
[Conan] Hmm, that would be
Uma Thurman, wouldn't it?

00:01:54.592 --> 00:01:55.850
I don't know who that is.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.557
Hmm, I'll take what you
said as meaning Uma Thurman.

00:01:59.557 --> 00:02:01.167
Do you know if she's
born in a summer month?

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.210
I don't know, she won't return my calls.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.718
Okay, let's get into it.

00:02:04.718 --> 00:02:06.750
Would you tell me your birthday?

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:10.750
April 18th, 4/18/63.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.580
[Psychic] Your minor number is a one

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.260
which means you're a
leader, not a follower.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.260
[Conan] Yes, I'm a leader.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.190
That's right, you are,
but your major number

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:22.103
is a five and five is the
number of communications.

00:02:23.293 --> 00:02:24.510
[Conan] May I ask you what
year you were born in?

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.190
1930.
You were born in 1930.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.454
Let me show you something right here.

00:02:28.454 --> 00:02:32.510
All right.
Okay, 1930, all right?

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.890
Okay.
Now, you said eight

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:38.157
is the number of power--
Power, money.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.610
Okay, eight goes into 19 how many times?

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.313
It goes in two, right?

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.750
Two you said was the number for growth.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.780
Action.
Action, all right.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.190
Yeah.
How many ones are there

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.780
in two?
Two.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.410
[Conan] That's two, but
there are two what's in two?

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:58.380
Two ones, that gives us a one.
(audience laughing)

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.320
I mean, one is your number, right?

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.450
Yeah.
The loneliest number.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.150
(audience laughing)
That's really different.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.330
I noticed something about your hand

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.570
which is very interesting.

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:09.116
Yeah, I'm putting Vaseline
on it, it's clearing up.

00:03:09.116 --> 00:03:10.403
No, this is--
Oh, this.

00:03:10.403 --> 00:03:11.976
[Velma] This is the Mount of Venus.

00:03:11.976 --> 00:03:12.809
[Conan] What does that mean?

00:03:12.809 --> 00:03:14.480
The mount of love, sympathy,

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.650
passion, virility, and sensuality.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.870
I like to call it love.
That's what it is.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.163
Yeah, mm. (growls seductively)

00:03:23.163 --> 00:03:24.960
Oh.
(audience laughing)

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.074
Should we go on?

00:03:26.074 --> 00:03:26.945
Mm, keep doing that.

00:03:26.945 --> 00:03:31.350
You like that, and notice it's
getting higher and higher.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:32.915
It's getting bigger and bigger.

00:03:32.915 --> 00:03:33.748
(audience laughing)

00:03:33.748 --> 00:03:35.990
How crass, oh Velma.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:36.823
How does this work?

00:03:36.823 --> 00:03:37.656
Do I--
You drink.

00:03:37.656 --> 00:03:39.660
I never, you drink the tea?
Mm-hmm.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.680
Then how do you read the tea leaves?

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.660
'Cause the tea leaves
will stay at the bottom.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:44.493
I'll show you.

00:03:44.493 --> 00:03:46.620
Oh, so I gotta drink the
whole cup of tea first

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.800
before we can even get started.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.023
Yeah.
Mm.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.660
Would you like some candies with it?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.090
You must enjoy it and also concentrate.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:55.430
I don't enjoy anything.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:57.570
I was raised Irish-Catholic,
I'm very uptight.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.422
What I see, with the
next three years mostly

00:04:00.422 --> 00:04:04.130
is a lot of parties and happy occasions,

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.010
that people are there and it's wild.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.420
Parties, I'm at parties?

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.720
Is James Caan there?

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.210
I don't see James Caan there.

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:11.815
[Conan] Okay, now your name is.

00:04:11.815 --> 00:04:13.688
Bahar.
Babar?

00:04:13.688 --> 00:04:16.210
Oh please, Bahar.
Bahar, I'm sorry.

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:17.800
I didn't know, I swear, I didn't--

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.287
Do I look like an elephant?
(audience laughing)

00:04:21.287 --> 00:04:24.000
That's interesting, there
are holy, magical cards

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.943
but you shuffle them just like
it's a cheap game of poker.

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.620
You will be will living--
(screams) Skull!

00:04:33.207 --> 00:04:36.913
Look at that! (screams)

00:04:36.913 --> 00:04:38.860
Look at that, what does that mean?

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.590
It's, that's, I don't know
much about tarot cards,

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.940
but you can't tell me one with
a big skull on it is good.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.431
That's gotta be a bad card.
No, it's a very good card.

00:04:47.431 --> 00:04:48.264
Really?

00:04:48.264 --> 00:04:50.070
[Bahar] Especially with medical students.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.580
You and your confounded jokes.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.950
So did you say I was gonna
be in a car accident, no?

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.448
I said be careful not to be.
Well, thank you.

00:04:58.448 --> 00:05:01.670
(audience laughing)
Gee, great, that's worth

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:02.980
whatever you're asking.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.670
What is all this stuff right here?

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.952
My home is my palace in reality.

00:05:06.952 --> 00:05:09.420
Does Major Healey know that you have this?

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:12.723
I would think he'd be
kind of upset, Jeannie!

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.210
This is my Aladdin's lamp.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:20.470
And in one of my magic acts
when I rub the lamp it did,

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.160
the Aladdin came out.
Wow, look at this.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.573
It's got a toggle switch.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.960
[Velma] Oh, now you're
giving away the secrets!

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.730
This is the early '60s version of it.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:30.563
Look at that right there.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.950
And we noticed when I came in here

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.500
there's a secret compartment here.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.333
That's a secret--

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:35.619
Where does this lead right now?

00:05:35.619 --> 00:05:36.989
[Velma] Don't open it, don't open it.

00:05:36.989 --> 00:05:38.500
[Conan] Where does it go,
why, is there someone in here?

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.967
[Velma] Oh gosh, don't open it!

00:05:40.967 --> 00:05:43.079
(psychedelic music)

00:05:43.079 --> 00:05:48.079
(screaming)
(audience laughing)

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:49.680
I want to look into the ball now

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.986
because I want you to tell me
the biggest thing in my life

00:05:51.986 --> 00:05:54.210
is my TV show.
Yes.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.670
It means everything to me.
Yes.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:58.440
And for a TV show to be successful

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.200
you have to get good guests.
Yes.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.620
And I want you to look
into the ball right now

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:06.440
and I want you to tell me,
what's the biggest guest

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:09.993
that I can expect to come on
my show in the next month?

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:15.363
Conan, I'll be appearing. (laughs)

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:22.640
We'll have fun, fun, fun.
(audience applauding)

00:06:23.802 --> 00:06:25.080
All right, well that was a lot of fun,

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.130
but I think we found out once and for all

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.860
that those fortune
tellers are way off base,

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.462
didn't we, Andy?
Yes, definitely.

00:06:32.462 --> 00:06:35.430
(screaming)
(audience applauding)

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:38.210
[Conan] (laughs) It's
Abe Vigoda, thanks, Abe!

